WEBVTT

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.820
That error yesterday was something, huh?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.160
It was totally unbelievable. That's why 
you should put me in from the benc—

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.450
Oww!

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.290
What an idiot.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.260
Calm down. Calm down.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.380
Looks like he's a little thinner 
than before, don't you think?

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.170
I wonder if he's getting enough to eat.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.930
If you're worried, why don't you take him in?

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.290
No way. If I take him home, 
I'll start to care for him.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.640
So why not just care for him, then?

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:16.230
Caring for things brings a lot of trouble.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.070
<i>The words Kou said that day...</i>

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:27.880
We're going to start negotiations. 
Come play with us in Barcelona.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.060
<i>He's laughing like he's having fun.</i>

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.200
<i>But maybe he doesn't really care 
about school or his friends?</i>

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.630
What? Mabuchi-kun said that?

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.730
Apparently, he spends a lot 
of his nights walking around.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.680
And he hangs out with people 
he doesn't seem to think of as friends.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.080
Futaba-chan... you really know him, huh?

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.260
I happened to do some investigating recently.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.320
I-Investigating?

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.190
He doesn't study, he just wanders around...

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.490
Did his midterms turn out okay, I wonder?

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.790
I don't think they did.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.290
Earlier, I saw Mabuchi and Tanaka-sensei...

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.250
Hey! Kou!

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.980
That's Tanaka-sensei's voice...

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:25.960
What's with you? Your midterm results... 
they're all below average!

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.640
If you don't turn it around soon, 
you won't advance to the next grade level.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.060
That's fine. I'll just quit school, then.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.690
Quit school? Listen, you...

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.400
If you do that, you'll definitely regret it.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:44.430
Will I...?

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.510
I'm kidding. Kidding.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.380
I think people who want to quit
 should just quit.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.170
But I don't like the way
 he makes Tanaka-sensei look.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.100
That brat!

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.870
But even if he was kidding, I don't 
like him talking about quitting.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.270
Mabuchi-kun...

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:22.530
The Leadership Workshop and the time 
he spent with all of us...

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.850
Doesn't he care about it, even a little?

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.250
I'm sure that Kou...

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.100
...has his own reasons 
for saying something so sad.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.170
I'm certain of it!

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:50.640
We just have to get so involved in his life 
that he won't say things like that anymore.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:56.850
I feel like, Futaba-chan... 
you've become really pretty lately.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.980
You were always cute, but...

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.570
Oh, really? You're making me blush!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.060
Actually, I put on makeup today!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.780
Oh, you really did.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.070
Yeah...

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:16.250
<i>I don't think it's just the makeup, though...</i>

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.650
<b>The Four Great World Civilizations 
Mesopotamian Civilization 
Egyptian Civilization 
Indus Civilization 
Yellow River Valley Civilization

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.440
Next up, I'll explain about the 
Yellow River Valley civilization,

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.540
one of the civilizations of ancient China.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.090
<i>I know he'll have fun if he's with us.</i>

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.130
Okay. Please open your textbooks to page 75.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.300
<i>I want Kou to feel that way.</i>

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.540
The Yellow River Valley Civilization 
could be called one of the

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.510
<i>How can we get Kou involved with us?</i>

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.130
world's four great civilizations.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:37.900
It was first born in the mid-stream 
Yellow River region around the year 5000 BC.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.090
The Yellow River Valley Civilization 
can be divided into two main periods,

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.590
early and late,

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.940
<b>What are you glaring at?</b>

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:49.200
based on two distinct 
differences in their culture.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.700
<b>I'm not glaring.</b>

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.460
<b>Wha? You're glaring as hard as you can! Ugly!</b>

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.710
<b>I said I'm not glaring! Cuebaaaall!</b>

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>I'm not a cueball! 
Peach is the cueball!!</b>

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.680
Peach

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.960
Let me see that.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.320
That's enough.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.170
How did it go?

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:35.310
Idiot. It's your fault he got mad at me.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.330
It's embarrassing.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.210
Huh? My fault?

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:41.920
You're the one who wrote 
"Peach is the cueball!!"

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.770
But he's totally bald!

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:42.900
Still
 here

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:43.900
Still
 here

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.130
Even if he is bald!

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:44.940
Still
 here

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.640
Is there something different about your face?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.780
I am wearing a little makeup...

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.560
Because of Kou

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.060
When someone who doesn't like to wear 
makeup starts wearing it, the reason is...

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.410
Love, right?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.380
Bullseye, huh?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.660
Kou. You say something, too.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.060
Even though you're just Yoshioka, 
you're acting awfully high and mighty.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:18.700
What's with that "Even though you're 
just Nobita" way of speaking?

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.410
You look like him, though.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.580
I wonder if Futaba-chan doesn't 
want to eat lunch yet?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.160
She does!

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:21.960
What?

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.580
You look like him.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:23.550
Like who?

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.450
Nobita.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.650
She seems a little preoccupied. 
Let's start eating without her.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:27.840
Hey! That's so rude!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:28.710
It's love, right?

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:29.430
What's that?

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:34.220
This? This is the CD I borrowed 
from Mabuchi-kun earlier!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:35.280
Who'd fall for you? Even though 
you're just Yoshioka.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:35.810
Shut up!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.710
Even though you're just Yoshioka.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.230
I told you—

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.370
Kou. I'm heading for the school store.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.220
Right. I'll go with you.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:45.690
You're running!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.400
I'm hungry.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.860
<i>No comment about the makeup, then...</i>

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.620
Kou? What's wrong?

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.030
It doesn't suit you.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.670
<i>Th-That's so mean!</i>

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:23.140
Don't come all the way back just 
to say something like that!

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.250
Kou, are you a croquette bread enthusiast? 
A yakisoba bread enthusiast?

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:37.740
If I've got to choose... yakisoba?

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:41.450
Me, too! The sensation of soba 
between bread really moves me!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.410
Mabuchi! It's been a while!

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.540
Hey.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.760
Friends of yours?

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:48.650
<i>Former</i> classmates.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.040
We haven't seen much of each other, have we?

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:57.150
I guess Mabuchi totally fits 
into the standard classes.

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:58.510
No sense that he's out of place.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.150
Thanks for your support.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.190
Oh! Are you in the advanced class?

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.920
That's right, Kou! You were in 
advanced classes last year, right?

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.350
I totally forgot about that! Wow!

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:14.330
Well, Mabuchi never fit in with the advanced 
classes, since he did so bad at tests.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.140
Standard classes make more sense.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:20.140
I spent all of our first year thinking, 
"Why's this kid in advanced classes?"

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.260
I know why, though!

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.190
You only got into advanced classes 
because you're related to Tanaka-sensei, right?

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:28.670
It stands to reason you couldn't keep up.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.670
I bet he was relieved when you stepped 
down to normal classes, right?

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.630
I bet he was!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:38.000
Hard for a teacher to save face when 
your little brother's flunking advanced classes.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.830
You guys. Knock it off already.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.130
You're persistent.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:50.510
It was just a joke...

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.940
Then you've got bad taste in jokes!

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.450
Calm down already. Why are you so mad?

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:58.570
Huh?!

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:03.370
They're saying crap about my friend! 
Why wouldn't I be mad?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.730
Let's go!

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.850
They're gone!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.690
Damn. They ran away.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.200
Those advanced class bas—

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.180
Those advanced class guys piss me off.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:23.430
I <i>seriously</i> hate guys like that.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.240
<i>I think... already...</i>

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.710
<i>They're... already...</i>

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:02.190
Makita?

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.120
Tanaka-sensei?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.100
What's wrong?

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.620
Mabuchi-kun...

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.120
Did something happen to Kou?

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:25.120
I heard he got bad scores on 
his midterms. Is that true?

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.160
That's private information, okay?

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.200
Does that mean you're worried about him?

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:37.750
A little.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:44.040
Kou's always been... a very stoic person.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:58.200
But with me...

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:11.330
He'd always call out "Brother, Brother" 
and rely on me unconditionally.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:16.730
Brother! Brother! It hurts!

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.570
You tried so hard!

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:24.600
Only with me...

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:33.540
But I guess he's got friends 
to worry about him now, huh?

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:35.710
I'm sure he'll try his hardest 
for all of you, too.

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:38.320
He'll be... fine.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:43.720
You'd better get inside. 
Lunch break's almost over.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:47.940
Okay...

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:01.710
Yuuri?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:06.430
To: Futaba-chan 
From: Yuuri

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:06.430
Do you think we could help 
Mabuchi-kun with his studies?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.440
<b>Mabuchi</b>

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.560
Kominato-kun.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.280
Yeah?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.990
This Saturday. Are you free?

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.920
Who in the world...?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.670
Oh, Kou? Where are you now?

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.190
Kominato? I'm at home...

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>Soft 
shredded 
squid</b>

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.400
I see! That's great!

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.770
Should we buy this?

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.650
We're having a study meeting 
at your house today!

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.650
Yeah, let's buy it!

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.860
I love that kind, too.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.860
We're heading over now!

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:08.730
Later.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.330
What's with that guy?

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:28.780
Did he say... a study meeting 
at my house? Was that a dream?

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:29.550
The lock!

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:33.640
The lock... the lock... the lock...

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.960
Dun da-dun!

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.940
Good morning, Mabuchi-kun!

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.970
Kou's room is really big, huh?

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:48.410
Yes. And so organized!

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.030
Shall we begin?

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.910
You hid all your dubious items, right?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.120
You didn't even give me time for that.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.460
That's right. Here.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:04.090
The CD you lent me. Thank you.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.010
We're all going to teach you 
about the subject we know best!

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.470
Huh? Teach me?

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:18.370
Yeah! Then you can lord it over 
those advanced class jerks.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.640
Then you'll repent to Tanaka-sensei.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.050
He's been really worried about you.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.340
No. Forget it.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.410
So uncooperative!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:36.890
<b>Anyone 
Can Do 
Science 
I-II</b>

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:36.890
<b>Easy to 
Understand 
Math II 
Problems</b>

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.290
If we do it together, even studying is fun!

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:41.080
Look! We brought potato chips, too!

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:42.420
<b>Potato chips 
Lightly Salted</b>

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.300
He's not getting lured in at all.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:49.740
Mabuchi-kun only just woke up. 
Maybe we're too energetic for him?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:54.300
Good point. Anyway, 
we're going to get started.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.070
Once your brain's awake, join us, okay?

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.790
Okay, someone good at math?

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:04.940
Oh, I'm pretty good at it.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.160
Well, there's this part 
I'd like you to explain to me...

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.570
Leave it to me! What part?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.460
Umm, let's see...

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:15.180
<i>This is bad. So annoying...</i>

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.010
This part, for me...

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.470
The same part for me.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.130
Where? Let me see, let me see...

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.780
This place, huh? Yeah.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.770
How do you do this part?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.090
This part? Let's see.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.770
Here, you do this...

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:42.420
Kominato-kun, please! 
The potato chip crumbs are falling!

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:44.290
They're getting on my notebook, too!

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.730
Ah! Crap!

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:05.170
These aren't consommé flavored.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.130
Mabuchi-kun woke up!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.590
You can't eat if you don't study!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.050
That's right! That's right!

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.050
Fine.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:18.730
Kominato. Move over a little.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.930
It's cramped.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.770
Hey! Don't push me, Kou.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.790
<i>All right! Kou joined us!</i>

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.360
<i>Lured in by the snacks.</i>

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.860
<i>Yes! This is going great!</i>

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:36.400
Mabuchi-kun. We have chocolate!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.330
Oh. Thank you.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.400
So? What's your specialty?

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:42.400
Science.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:45.220
Oh? I wouldn't expect that.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:46.780
I hear that a lot.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.880
Well, teach me, Sensei.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:55.750
<i>I feel like he's making fun of me, but...</i>

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:00.100
Hurry. Hurry.

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.030
<i>Why does it tug at my heart?! 
Does this mean I'm a pervert?</i>

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:08.270
I can start from the problems 
on the midterm, right?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.210
I'm going to sleep if you don't hurry.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.020
Wait a minute!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.220
Um! Mabuchi-kun!

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:20.870
Could you bring glasses for everyone?

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:20.870
<b>Tea</b>

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.100
Oh. Sure.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.740
I'll get them.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:27.580
I'll look for some examples 
on that level while you're gone.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:48.270
Are you okay? Can I help?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:54.120
Oh, sorry. I haven't used these in a while,
 so I wanted to get them clean.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.470
I'll dry, then.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:57.780
Thanks.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.280
Then here.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.160
Okay.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:06.890
Here.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:07.620
Okay.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:14.520
Here.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.270
Okay.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.660
Mabuchi-kun, listen...

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.680
About Futaba-chan...

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:25.680
Do you l—

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:30.410
<i>What if...</i>

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.340
Huh? What?

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.750
I couldn't hear you because of the water.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:38.030
Say it again?

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:43.020
<i>If he admits he likes Futaba-chan... 
what will I do?</i>

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.490
Makita?

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.740
Sorry. It's nothing.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.590
Well, I'll take these for now.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:58.530
I'm sorry! I kicked the bag!

00:19:58.530 --> 00:19:59.770
Clumsy.

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:01.260
I'll pick them right up!

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.000
You didn't hurt your foot?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.940
No, I'm okay!

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.900
Honestly, who brought potatoes?

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:41.590
Those two are taking a while.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.910
I'm going to check on them.

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:45.980
Have a good trip!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:53.020
Murao-sama! Teach me English!

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.570
Fine.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:03.080
Kou? Yuuri?

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.130
Oh, there you are.

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:10.490
What happened? You're taking so long.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.700
But where's Yuuri?

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:25.750
We weren't doing anything.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:33.970
Did something happen... with Kou?

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:44.520
Nothing at all.

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:51.280
<i>That doesn't feel like... "nothing at all"...</i>

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:40.940
Next Episode . . .

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:32.000
With most people, if you talk 
to them a certain amount,

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:36.430
then start to avoid them, 
they won't try to get involved anymore.

00:23:37.510 --> 00:23:39.560
You're really something.
